  "timelapse": 0.04,
  "steps": [
    {
      "say": "This is a hand-crank egg beater. You hold the top handle, turn the red knob on the big wheel, and the two metal beaters at the bottom whirl around to whip eggs or cream.",
      "do": [
        {
          "reveal": [
            "frame",
            "handle",
            "crank_wheel",
            "pinion_left",
            "pinion_right",
            "beater_left",
            "beater_right"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "all"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "Everything hangs on the frame, a strong metal bar. The handle on top is where you hold it steady, like holding a flashlight pointing down.",
      "do": [
        {
          "label": [
            "frame",
            "handle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "frame",
            "handle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "frame"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "Your hand turns the crank wheel. The red knob sits on an arm fixed to the big wheel, so every time your hand goes around once, the whole wheel goes around once.",
      "do": [
        {
          "label": [
            "crank_wheel"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "crank_wheel"
          ]
        },
        {
          "spin": [
            "crank_wheel"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "crank_wheel"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "Look through the big wheel. It has teeth on its back face, and they catch two small gears. The small gears are much smaller, so they spin several times for every turn of the big wheel, like a little bike wheel racing to keep up.",
      "do": [
        {
          "cutaway": [
            "crank_wheel"
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": [
            "pinion_left",
            "pinion_right"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "pinion_left",
            "pinion_right"
          ]
        },
        {
          "spin": [
            "crank_wheel"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "crank_wheel"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "One small gear is caught at the bottom of the big wheel and the other at the top, so they turn opposite ways. That is how the two beaters spin against each other.",
      "do": [
        {
          "explode": "all"
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "crank_wheel",
            "pinion_left",
            "pinion_right"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "all"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "Each small gear has a long shaft, and a beater sits on the end. The curved blades slice through the egg and fold in air bubbles, which makes it fluffy.",
      "do": [
        {
          "label": [
            "beater_left",
            "beater_right"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "beater_left",
            "beater_right"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "beater_left"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "Now let's put it all back together and give it a spin. One slow turn of your hand becomes fast whirling beaters!",
      "do": [
        {
          "explode": []
        },
        {
          "spin": [
            "crank_wheel"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "all"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "recap": "An egg beater uses a big gear to turn two small gears fast, so a slow turn of the crank makes the beaters whirl quickly in opposite directions.",
  "question": "What else do you think uses a big gear and a small gear to make something spin faster?",
